  "prefLabel": "Plc 1305.08 Initial Licenses: Issuance and Duration",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1305.08 Initial Licenses: Issuance and Duration.\n\n(a) Each initial license issued under this chapter shall specify:\n\n(1) The name of the licensee;\n\n(2) The effective date of the license;\n\n(3) The license number; and\n\n(4) The regulated MIRT profession in which the licensee is licensed.\n\n(b) An initial license shall:\n\n(1) Expire 2 years from the date on which the license was issued unless a timely and complete renewal application is filed or the license is sooner suspended or revoked in accordance with Plc 1311; and\n\n(2) Be subject to renewal.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Plc 1300) #13701, eff 8-1-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1300.html"
